{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1343668-story-seeds-forsaken-edition","id":1343668,"title":"Story Seeds-Forsaken Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-25T15:22:55-07:00","id":1343668,"title":"Story Seeds-Forsaken Edition","content":"Couldn't find a thread for this, so I figured I'd start one up. Maybe I missed it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I mainly bring this up because one of the idle ideas that crossed my mind is that there's a clamoring for the era where in the Forsaken made their pacts with the Firstborn, and I think it's actually fairly spread out, but an idea for one particular instance popped into my head, and I suppose all I need is a historical period to work with.<br /> <br /> Namely, it's an era that would somewhat challenge the mythos of Werewolf in that it's a point of Winter and Famine that is sparked by the Wolves Destroyer, Dire, and Winter are out to end the world between The Sundered World and the Fall of Bau. The era would be, in game terms at least, be marked at the end by the Tribal Oaths of one of the Three(I'm leaning towards Destroyer, but it could be any combination of three, including all of them, or maybe even Dire has already made his). I like something of the survivalist/near-apocalypse setting meshing with the foundational spirit politics of Forsaken's setting, and making the trio more complex.<br /> <br /> Anyways, any thoughts on that, or any idle/active story seeds of your own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T16:07:49-07:00","id":1343677,"title":"","content":"A story I ran involved a Sorrow ridden individual going around to various dive bars and draining the saddest people they could find. Witnesses only remembered seeing a guy comforting the victim, whom was left with missing eyes when it was all said and done. (The eyes remained intact just all the liquid was drained out, they literally cried them out)<br /> <br /> The setting I used was Bowery Dogs for that grindhouse feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T23:33:22-07:00","id":1343724,"title":"","content":"You could add these to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lf-story-hooks</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},